        },
        {
          "extraction_class": "individual_diagnostics",
          "extraction_text": "Needle EMG showed increased volitional activity and poor relaxation, particularly in the right tibialis anterior and lumbosacral paraspinal muscles in association with severe spasm. A lumbar puncture for anti-glutamic acid decarboxylase (anti-GAD) antibodies was done. (Several months after discharge, a positive result was obtained.)",
